# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/prdoc/master/prdoc_schema_user.json

title: 'sp-arithmetic: make compact encoding bounds explicit'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `BaseArithmetic` and the signed-or-unsigned arithmetic traits no longer imply SCALE compact
      encoding. Compact encoding remains required on the unsigned arithmetic traits and on the
      call sites that actually compact-encode values.

      This allows signed integer types to satisfy the general arithmetic traits while keeping the
      existing compact-encoding requirements explicit. Downstream generic code that relied on
      `BaseArithmetic` or `AtLeast32Bit` implying `HasCompact` should add an explicit
      `HasCompact` bound, or use the appropriate unsigned arithmetic trait when compact encoding
      is required.

crates:
  - name: sp-arithmetic
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-timestamp
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-indices
    bump: major
  - name: bp-runtime
    bump: major
